# Each additional triggering is a triggering (CR 603.2d), so "This ability triggers only once each turn" (CR 603.2h)
# counts it: Enduring Innocence's "Whenever one or more other creatures you control with power 2 or less enter, draw a
# card" triggers once for an Ornithopter entering under Panharmonicon, not twice, and not again for a second Ornithopter
# that turn. On turn 5 it triggers again, once: the limit is the turn's.
# Hand: 7 - 4 played on turn 1 = 3; turn 3 draws a Plains (4), plays it, Enduring Innocence and both Ornithopters (0),
# draws one (1); turn 5 draws the third Ornithopter (2), casts it (1), draws one (2).

